# What must never enter the frontend build context.
#
# This one is a correctness fix, not just a size one. The Dockerfile runs
# `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`, so a host `node_modules/` in the context is
# copied straight over the one the image just installed - handing a Linux
# container the native binaries (sharp, unrs-resolver, fsevents) that npm built
# for the developer's macOS. A stale host `.next/` does the same to the build
# output.

node_modules/
.next/
out/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
coverage/
